<title>VENEZUELA: TABLE-Madosa 9-month shr lower.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Madosa 9-month shr lower.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shr 23.52 bolivars vs 72.39 bolivars</p>
<p>Net 543 million bolivars vs 1.670 billion bolivars</p>
<p>Sales 27.919 billion bolivars vs 21.098 billion bolivars</p>
<p>Cost of sales 22.737 billion bolivars vs 16.147 billion bolivars</p>
<p>Oper income 1.118 billion bolivars vs 2.161 billion bolivars</p>
<p>Financing costs 390.408 million bolivars vs 420.498 million bolivars</p>
<p>NOTES: Nine month period to June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>Results are not inflation-adjusted.</p>
<p>Madosa is a domestic appliances manufacturer. Enron Corp holds a 42 percent share and General Electric Co 33 percent.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
</text>
